{
	"note": "Carrying (Dave 2026-10-20, changed 2026-10-21): weight in KILOGRAMS of ONE item (one stone, one stick, one gathered handful or piece), and a stack weighs count x that, in the carry total, the sort and the UI (shown in grams under 1 kg). Audited 2026-10-21 against real mass: plant fibre a few grams, a handful of leaves 20 g, berries 50 g, a mushroom cap 50 g, a root 250 g, a 2 m stick 400 g, a hand stone 1 kg, a bolt of split firewood 3.5 kg (a log of 15 kg splits into four), driftwood 4 kg, a short log 15 kg (a half-metre bolt, what one person can lift), wood pieces 2 kg, tools by material (stone axe 1.0, knife 0.2, spear 0.8, wooden spear and spade 0.4 and 0.8). A crafted item is never heavier than what went into it, and a kit weighs what it is made of (campfire 10 stones and 20 sticks, 18 kg). Everything not listed falls to default_kg. by_id wins over by_suffix (an item id that ends with the word, first match in the order written); the most a body carries is carry_kg_per_body_kg x body weight (placeholder for strength; the server refuses to pick up more). Up to free_ratio (80 percent) of that limit nothing hinders at all: full speed, no extra effort. Above it you slow smoothly down to min_speed at the limit, and load_effort x fraction^load_effort_power (fraction 0 at 80 percent of the limit to 1 at the limit) is added to the effort of a moving player. Species logs (log_<species>, Dave 2026-10-21) are large logs carried on the shoulder, one at a time: by_id kg per species group (hardwood 45, softwood 32, light 26), counted in the carried weight so the walk slows by the usual rules.",
